{"id": "en_wildfire_road_p2", "total": 71.11, "segments": [{"text": "Part two. Dan reaches his car on the trail just as severe fire traps the vehicle completely tonight.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.82}, {"text": "Official safety experts emphasize that waiting to evacuate is always the absolute most dangerous choice available.", "start": 6.48, "end": 11.4}, {"text": "But since Dan is already trapped, staying inside his car is safer than running on foot.", "start": 11.84, "end": 16.32}, {"text": "One.", "start": 16.07, "end": 16.09}, {"text": "Immediately park your vehicle in an open area that is entirely clear of dry ground vegetation.", "start": 18.4, "end": 22.34}, {"text": "Keep the engine running continuously so essential safety systems and bright vehicle lights stay fully powered.", "start": 23.18, "end": 27.88}, {"text": "Two.", "start": 27.610000000000003, "end": 27.063}, {"text": "Tightly close all car windows and heating vents to block dangerous toxic smoke from entering quickly.", "start": 29.72, "end": 33.86}, {"text": "Toxic dark smoke will rapidly enter the passenger space if vents remain open to outside air.", "start": 34.38, "end": 38.5}, {"text": "Three.", "start": 38.29, "end": 37.561}, {"text": "Get down low on the floorboard to shield your entire body from extreme radiant fire heat.", "start": 40.36, "end": 43.78}, {"text": "Cover yourself completely with a thick wool blanket or heavy winter jacket to prevent painful burns.", "start": 44.44, "end": 48.2}, {"text": "Dan crouches low on the floorboard as intense orange flames sweep across the dusty mountain road.", "start": 49.06, "end": 53.02}, {"text": "The strong metal vehicle frame shields him while the roaring forest fire sweeps past his position.", "start": 53.02, "end": 57.72}, {"text": "Dan survives the terrifying blaze because he executed every critical vehicle safety rule with absolute precision.", "start": 58.46, "end": 63.6}, {"text": "Always stay inside your vehicle when trapped. Follow for a new survival scenario tomorrow.", "start": 64.2, "end": 67.96}], "words": [["Part", 0.0, 0.42], ["two.", 0.261, 0.522], ["Dan", 1.72, 1.9], ["reaches", 1.9, 2.12], ["his", 2.12, 2.34], ["car", 2.34, 2.5], ["on", 2.5, 2.62], ["the", 2.62, 2.7], ["trail", 2.7, 2.92], ["just", 2.92, 3.26], ["as", 3.26, 3.48], ["severe", 3.48, 3.8], ["fire", 3.8, 4.18], ["traps", 4.18, 4.54], ["the", 4.54, 4.66], ["vehicle", 4.66, 4.88], ["completely", 4.88, 5.36], ["tonight.", 5.36, 5.82], ["Official", 6.48, 6.78], ["safety", 6.78, 7.04], ["experts", 7.04, 7.4], ["emphasize", 7.4, 7.82], ["that", 7.82, 8.08], ["waiting", 8.08, 8.32], ["to", 8.32, 8.54], ["evacuate", 8.54, 8.92], ["is", 8.92, 9.18], ["always", 9.18, 9.58], ["the", 9.58, 9.82], ["absolute", 9.82, 10.26], ["most", 10.26, 10.56], ["dangerous", 10.56, 10.8], ["choice", 10.8, 11.04], ["available.", 11.04, 11.4], ["But", 11.84, 12.06], ["since", 12.06, 12.34], ["Dan", 12.34, 12.54], ["is", 12.54, 12.68], ["already", 12.68, 12.9], ["trapped,", 12.9, 13.24], ["staying", 13.72, 13.88], ["inside", 13.88, 14.42], ["his", 14.42, 14.68], ["car", 14.68, 14.94], ["is", 14.94, 15.2], ["safer", 15.2, 15.5], ["than", 15.5, 15.7], ["running", 15.7, 15.92], ["on", 15.92, 16.06], ["foot.", 16.06, 16.32], ["One.", 16.07, 16.09], ["Immediately", 18.4, 18.74], ["park", 18.74, 19.06], ["your", 19.06, 19.22], ["vehicle", 19.22, 19.5], ["in", 19.5, 19.66], ["an", 19.66, 19.78], ["open", 19.78, 20.0], ["area", 20.0, 20.3], ["that", 20.3, 20.46], ["is", 20.46, 20.54], ["entirely", 20.54, 20.98], ["clear", 20.98, 21.28], ["of", 21.28, 21.5], ["dry", 21.5, 21.72], ["ground", 21.72, 21.94], ["vegetation.", 21.94, 22.34], ["Keep", 23.18, 23.48], ["the", 23.48, 23.64], ["engine", 23.64, 23.8], ["running", 23.8, 24.04], ["continuously", 24.04, 24.7], ["so", 24.7, 24.96], ["essential", 24.96, 25.24], ["safety", 25.24, 25.58], ["systems", 25.58, 25.88], ["and", 25.88, 26.02], ["bright", 26.02, 26.24], ["vehicle", 26.24, 26.56], ["lights", 26.56, 26.76],